{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G1 and G2 model the robot's perception (obstacle and path sensing) and motion command execution, respectively. The specification automata E1 and E2 enforce safe, coverage-oriented exploration: E1 binds sensor outcomes to the appropriate motion actions, prioritizing forward progress and random_walk in clear conditions, and using short directed turns or rare backward escapes for obstacle recovery. E2 prevents repeated rotation or backward actions, ensuring the robot returns to exploration as soon as possible and does not get stuck in recovery loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (G1) and motion (G2) to cleanly model uncontrollable sensor outcomes and controllable motion commands.",
    "Specification automata E1 and E2 bind perception to safe, progress-maximizing actions, enforce conservative recovery, and prevent repeated recovery actions, ensuring steady exploration and reliable obstacle avoidance."
  ],
